<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chang Jun</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">7th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chang Jun was a Chinese official sent by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-yang-of-sui">Emperor Yang</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sui-dynasty">Sui dynasty</a> in 607 as envoy to Chi Tu, the &quot;Red Earth&quot; kingdom of South-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-asia">East Asia</a>. He sailed from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guangzhou">Guangzhou</a> with Wang Junzheng, and his report, preserved in the Book of Sui, describes Chi Tu's court, its Buddhist and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brahmins">Brahmin</a> rites and its customs. He returned to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> in 610 with an envoy from Chi Tu.</p></div>
